# Auth sidecar wiring for the dashboard's Caddy site block.
#
# PHASE 1 (audit mode) — NOT wired into request flow.
#   Just run ac-organic-lab-auth.service (loopback :8009) with
#   AUTH_ENFORCE=false and confirm identity extraction out-of-band:
#
#     curl -s -H 'X-Forwarded-For: <a-human-device-tailnet-ip>' \
#       http://127.0.0.1:8009/auth/verify | python3 -m json.tool
#     journalctl -u ac-organic-lab-auth -f      # watch resolved identities
#
#   Nothing is gated; this only proves `whois` resolves real users before we
#   lean on it.
#
# PHASE 2 (enforce) — add the block below INSIDE the dashboard site block,
# set AUTH_ENFORCE=true on the sidecar, and have control.py read X-Auth-User.
# forward_auth only guards the mutating control routes; reads stay open. The
# action-name + kind bypasses (lights, camera, env) still live in the app /
# Next.js middleware — Caddy handles the broad surface here.
#
#   @control {
#       path /api/equipment/*/control/*
#       method POST PUT PATCH DELETE
#   }
#   forward_auth @control 127.0.0.1:8009 {
#       uri /auth/verify
#       copy_headers X-Auth-User X-Auth-Display X-Auth-Tagged
#   }
#
# Caddy populates X-Forwarded-For with the client's Tailnet IP, which is what
# the sidecar resolves. Pin trusted_proxies before relying on it for enforcement.
